course: dictionary
lesson: 8729
title: Sequences: things in order
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sequence is a set of things that come one after another in a certain order. Getting dressed is a sequence: socks before trainers. «Sequence is the order of instructions, and changing the order changes what happens.» Put the steps in a new order and the result can go wrong.
explain: In maths, a number sequence follows a rule. Look at 2, 4, 6, 8. Each number is the one before plus 2, so the next number is 10. The rule is the link between the numbers, and finding it helps you predict what comes next.
explain: Each number in a sequence has a place, called a term. The first term is the first number, the second term is the second number, and so on. «The next number in the sequence» means the number that comes straight after the last one you can see.
explain: Sequences also show up in stories and computing. «A script runs from top to bottom, one block after another, and this order is called a sequence.» If the events of a story are out of sequence, the story makes less sense.
fact: A sequence is a set of things that come one after another in a certain order.
fact: «In sequence» means in order; «out of sequence» means mixed up.
fact: In a number sequence, each term follows a rule, such as adding 2 each time.
fact: A script runs from top to bottom, one block after another, and this order is called a sequence.
fact: Stars spend about 90% of their lives steadily fusing hydrogen into helium, a stage astronomers call the main sequence.
exercise: What comes next in the sequence 2, 4, 6, 8? | 12 | 9 | 16 | *10
exercise: Which list is in sequence for getting dressed? | *Socks, then trainers, then go out | Trainers, then socks, then go out | Go out, then socks, then trainers
exercise: The pictures of a story are mixed up. What do you need to put them back in? | Their colours | *Their sequence, the order they happen in | Their sizes | A bigger page
test: Astronomers call a stage in a star's life, when it steadily fuses hydrogen, what? | Black hole | Shooting star | *Main sequence | Red giant
test: Find the next term in the sequence 3, 6, 9, 12 | 13 | 14 | *15 | 21
exam: What is the rule for the sequence 1, 3, 5, 7? | Multiply by 2 each time | *Add 2 each time | Add 1 each time | Take away 2 each time
